=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/System (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/System   kind=page   web route=(unrouted)
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/SystemPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + maui-windows workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free, unit-tested
  headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view),
  exactly as the sibling W7 ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "SystemPage.xaml + SystemPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real
  conventions (namespace TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Admin).
- The web SystemPage is a thin shell: a PageContainer title/subtitle header above a <Stack className="gap-6">
  holding two presentational panels — RateLimitStatusPanel then QueueStatusPanel — and it owns NO query
  (manifest: "no API data sources - renders from navigation params / local state"). The native SystemPage
  reproduces this exactly: SystemPage.cs composes the two ALREADY-IMPLEMENTED sibling panels
  (feature-views/RateLimitStatusPanel.cs, feature-views/QueueStatusPanel/QueueStatusPanel.cs) inside a
  ScrollViewer + StackPanel(Spacing=24) under a PageTitle + Subhead header bound to SystemPageViewModel.
- The two web GlassPanel regions ARE the two embedded panels; each carries its own loading / empty / error
  state holder (RateLimitStatusViewModel / QueueStatusViewModel), so the three data states render inside the
  panels precisely as the web composes them. SystemPage adds no data state of its own (parity-correct).
- Navigation (ADR): the web page exports SYSTEM_PAGE_PATH '/admin/system' but is NEVER referenced by any web
  router (verified: only SystemPage.tsx mentions it), so the manifest web route is (unrouted) and the native
  Core/Navigation/RouteTable.cs intentionally carries NO matching entry (it ports web <Route>s 1:1). The W4
  ShellPageFactory is still given the page by route name ("System") in ShellWindow.xaml.cs so the surface is
  reachable by deep link / programmatic navigation without inventing a route the web baseline lacks.
- Default data sources: the shell constructs the page through its parameterless ctor, which (mirroring the
  ApiLogsPage/FeedbackQueuePage EmptyFeed precedent) binds the two panels to EmptyRateLimitStatusSource /
  EmptyQueueStatusSource. Each yields a single RepositoryResult<…>.Empty() emission so the panels resolve to
  their empty state — never an indefinite spinner — until a host wires the repository-backed sources through
  the panels' Create(IApiClient, …) factory. No HTTP touches the view.
- i18n: both manifest keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names. system.page.title was
  already present in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (translation.system.page.title = "System budgets");
  system.page.subtitle was MISSING and was added to all three catalogs
  (translation.system.page.subtitle = "Operator dashboard for the throttles and budgets that bound this
  TeslaSync deployment.", English in ar/he per the existing untranslated convention), inserted in
  alphabetical order before the .title row.
- Pre-existing blocker repaired: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been re-corrupted by its documented
  .gitattributes merge=union strategy into TWO <Project> roots + TWO PropertyGroups + duplicated item groups
  (2633 Compile items, only 1327 distinct), failing XML load (MSB4025: multiple root elements @1380) and
  blocking the whole-solution build at baseline. Regenerated into the single canonical Project root the file's
  own INVARIANT mandates: case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated union of every
  Microsoft.UI-free source (1327 distinct) plus the two new SystemPage Model/ViewModel links (1329 total), LF
  + final newline. No linked source dropped; PackageReference/ProjectReference/Content sets preserved.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=2

# Panels (2) — the two web GlassPanel regions, reproduced as the embedded W3 panels in web order
[x] panel  - RateLimitStatusPanel -> SystemPage.cs#BuildLayout adds new RateLimitStatusPanel(rateLimitSource, localizer)
             (web <Stack> child 1); owns its loading/empty/error/stale/offline state via RateLimitStatusViewModel.
[x] panel  - QueueStatusPanel     -> SystemPage.cs#BuildLayout adds new QueueStatusPanel(queueSource, localizer)
             (web <Stack> child 2); owns its loading/empty/error/stale/offline state via QueueStatusViewModel.

# Data states — the page owns none (no data source); the embedded panels render all three, driven here to empty
[x] state  - empty (default) -> EmptyRateLimitStatusSource / EmptyQueueStatusSource yield RepositoryResult<…>.Empty();
             test Empty_sources_drive_the_panels_to_their_empty_state asserts RateLimitPanelState.Empty + QueuePanelState.Empty.

# Strings (2) — every visible literal resolves from Strings/*.resw via ILocalizer with the web key names
[x] string - system.page.subtitle -> SystemPageRegistration.Subtitle (SystemPage.Model.cs) localizer.GetString(
             "system.page.subtitle", "Operator dashboard for the throttles and budgets that bound this TeslaSync deployment.");
             surfaced by SystemPageViewModel.Subtitle (SystemPage.ViewModel.cs) and rendered by SystemPage.cs#_subtitleText (Subhead);
             catalog row translation.system.page.subtitle ADDED to Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw;
             tests ViewModel_resolves_every_required_string_key + Registration_exposes_the_web_default_strings.
[x] string - system.page.title    -> SystemPageRegistration.Title (SystemPage.Model.cs) localizer.GetString(
             "system.page.title", "System budgets"); surfaced by SystemPageViewModel.Title and rendered by
             SystemPage.cs#_titleText (PageTitle); catalog row translation.system.page.title present in
             Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; tests ViewModel_resolves_every_required_string_key +
             Registration_exposes_the_web_default_strings.

